# bao1x_iox_gpio_test.resc -- real, verified round-trip test for the
# IOX GPIO behavioral model (renode/iox_gpio.repl), per baoregon-trail
# issue #2.
#
# Loads src/main_renode_iox_test.c's ELF (polls IOX's real
# SFR_GPIOIN_SRGI1 input register), runs it briefly to observe the
# initial LOW state, then directly writes a HIGH bit into the same
# register via `sysbus WriteDoubleWord` (simulating an external pin
# transition -- the legitimate stand-in for a real button press, since
# this model has no real external pin wiring), then runs again to
# confirm the firmware's own poll loop picks up the transition.
#
# Usage (from the repo root):
#   renode --console --disable-xwt renode/bao1x_iox_gpio_test.resc

using sysbus

mach create "bao1x-iox-test"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/bao1x.repl

sysbus LoadELF @build-renode-iox/iox_test.elf

emulation RunFor "0.01"

# Real IOX SFR_GPIOIN_SRGI1 register address: base 0x5012f000 + offset
# 0x17c (port PB input value, per bao1x_peri.svd / iox.rs). Set bit 3
# (TEST_PIN in main_renode_iox_test.c) HIGH -- this is the simulated
# "button press".
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x5012f17c 0x00000008

emulation RunFor "0.01"
